r-fields ["q-86733/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "144d1258-f8d5-55e9-be38-ec25b6f84bd3"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-86733"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-81196/selection/6189ad81c7182dd8b8b6e80740736c0507433c1ec125f9fe44c205386912ad85" :answer/id #uuid "3eed2c63-6931-54c5-92fb-c4f19935d8b3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-81196/selection/0b7717428db23ef825997cdc5ccbdaecdb3bb5faa46312d3f714f6aa9a4c16cb" :answer/id #uuid "60fd872f-404f-5562-99ef-a64931cd8557" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-81196/selection/c8e69750579eb4c84d9ea108d14211c2620e308d86f4adb194007c0d6717f9e5" :answer/id #uuid "11a6c226-cdcc-542a-99b4-23a96264a863" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ 1 \\\\ \\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-81196/selection/5ab39819bd591bb7ae04b7985a07f0432cc31fc28508b220c8ad02bc64cb63c1" :answer/id #uuid "c8e03b9b-61aa-57c8-9e2f-578844db2c87" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-81196/selection/1bdf5962f0ad0ad875680ad15bc14f2b96de33f4a1b713d05135e038ae7b7260" :answer/id #uuid "cb87f663-5ccd-54db-80bf-2809b22507ab" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-81196/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "184ce97b-ec25-52e6-a5f4-d63b5ebd5d94" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-81196/selection/0b7717428db23ef825997cdc5ccbdaecdb3bb5faa46312d3f714f6aa9a4c16cb" :answer-field/choices ["q-81196/selection/6189ad81c7182dd8b8b6e80740736c0507433c1ec125f9fe44c205386912ad85" "q-81196/selection/0b7717428db23ef825997cdc5ccbdaecdb3bb5faa46312d3f714f6aa9a4c16cb" "q-81196/selection/c8e69750579eb4c84d9ea108d14211c2620e308d86f4adb194007c0d6717f9e5" "q-81196/selection/5ab39819bd591bb7ae04b7985a07f0432cc31fc28508b220c8ad02bc64cb63c1" "q-81196/selection/1bdf5962f0ad0ad875680ad15bc14f2b96de33f4a1b713d05135e038ae7b7260"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-81196" :question/id #uuid "f7628d96-7413-59a8-b813-69718d9f2735" :question/math-academy-id "q-81196" :question/problem "Given the vector $x$ and the system of linear equations below, find the projection of $x$ onto the solution space of the system.\n\n$$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}],\\,{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=0 \\\\ 2{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}=0\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to find a basis of the solution space of the system. \n\nConsider the augmented matrix $M$ of the system, which we reduce to row echelon form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn the reduced matrix above, there are $2$ pivot columns ($1$st and $2$nd). Thus, ${x}_{3}$ is a free variable. Now, from the second equation, we get ${x}_{2}={x}_{3}.$ Substituting this into the first equation, we obtain \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}+{x}_{3}=0\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=-{x}_{3}.\n$$\n\nSo, the general solution is\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]={x}_{3}[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{3}\\in R.\n$$\n\nConsequently, $B={[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]}$ is a basis of the solution space of the system.\n\nFinally, we find the projection of $x$ onto the solution space of the system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{b}\\,x & =\\frac{x\\cdot b}{b\\cdot b}b \\\\  & =\\frac{(-2)\\cdot (-1)+3\\cdot 1+7\\cdot 1}{(-1)^{2}+{1}^{2}+{1}^{2}}b \\\\  & =\\frac{12}{3}b \\\\  & =4b \\\\  & =4[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-81196/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f8d8c7fb-e69a-5b52-9566-4d2e0c7e54fc"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-81196"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-81199/selection/03f928726c1be7e1704d9012ef3b71570a37993dcd22b7ac522852cc90e2d1e8" :answer/id #uuid "69c2f9d8-51e9-556e-8204-c724a3d5d84f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-81199/selection/fc4e2cf106841016abafd2875d67ff73af65a59d2ae61b8b12fe8b80bbbe07ac" :answer/id #uuid "3b9c687c-4b48-5748-9143-c39279e56106" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-81199/selection/7cf029c3ab18e89829906bc75ea8bccab0149c53f5ce25583e1200fd91e8d36e" :answer/id #uuid "1d5869a3-9c6c-5144-8b07-a2e8fc425c06" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-81199/selection/c4d0e168a3d99e885148b89f97a23513d303c5fe482984e986cd451f839bd066" :answer/id #uuid "1f793a48-dfbf-5c20-a8c5-e0dbe63606c8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-81199/selection/b70163afa80242b6e07599db9e6649592c88c8df8d6892329736a0a5f2ef7d0f" :answer/id #uuid "03e1163e-b88d-5484-b4a3-68cbf39c712a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-81199/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "0585e468-45e4-50cc-86a1-46acd21d4bcc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-81199/selection/fc4e2cf106841016abafd2875d67ff73af65a59d2ae61b8b12fe8b80bbbe07ac" :answer-field/choices ["q-81199/selection/03f928726c1be7e1704d9012ef3b71570a37993dcd22b7ac522852cc90e2d1e8" "q-81199/selection/fc4e2cf106841016abafd2875d67ff73af65a59d2ae61b8b12fe8b80bbbe07ac" "q-81199/selection/7cf029c3ab18e89829906bc75ea8bccab0149c53f5ce25583e1200fd91e8d36e" "q-81199/selection/c4d0e168a3d99e885148b89f97a23513d303c5fe482984e986cd451f839bd066" "q-81199/selection/b70163afa80242b6e07599db9e6649592c88c8df8d6892329736a0a5f2ef7d0f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-81199" :question/id #uuid "bcc8ff8e-bf46-5901-8fed-da7d7df3ad36" :question/math-academy-id "q-81199" :question/problem "Given the vector $x$ and the system of linear equations below, find the projection of $x$ onto the solution space of the system.\n\n$$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}],\\,{\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{1}-{x}_{2}=0 \\\\ -{x}_{1}+\\frac{1}{2}{x}_{2}=0\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to find a basis of the solution space of the system. \n\nConsider the augmented matrix $M$ of the system, which we reduce to row echelon form, as follows:  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & \\frac{1}{2} & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn the reduced matrix above, there is $1$ pivot column (the $1$st one). Thus, ${x}_{2}$ is a free variable. From the first equation, we get ${x}_{1}=\\frac{1}{2}{x}_{2}.$ So, the general solution is\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2}{x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]={x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{2}\\in R.\n$$\n\nConsequently, $B={[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]}$ is a basis of the solution space of the system.\n\nFinally, we find the projection of $x$ onto the solution space of the system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{b}\\,x & =\\frac{x\\cdot b}{b\\cdot b}b \\\\  & =\\frac{4\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}+3\\cdot 1}{{(\\frac{1}{2})}^{2}+{1}^{2}}b \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{\\frac{1}{4}+1}b \\\\  & =4b \\\\  & =4[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-81199/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f8d8c7fb-e69a-5b52-9566-4d2e0c7e54fc"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-81199"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-81200/selection/d75933ccdef909be74ce3d210a4b508b4ae0f3c90e8b68aa102024366905c0a6" :answer/id #uuid "918ae809-248d-561f-8236-5fe0c1b51f5e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-81200/selection/1fbf95c252312fea464880d0146235c2d254085faaec63a5ef8fe17552495710" :answer/id #uuid "9ee4b450-5be0-53a9-99a0-22e008127944" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}12 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-81200/selection/a3f9576cd5e49b32680167e2d19cb3084db80cef51740e2c74eee8b8d9070598" :answer/id #uuid "c437f2dd-4de5-5439-88ad-ceba0f35ea1c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}12 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-81200/selection/b94ad2ce8b17f182e799d872f345298a72a9b827c3051416e0b84910de3366fc" :answer/id #uuid "1c9fefc9-f782-5e47-8f7e-3d17727c9f9d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-12 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-81200/selection/c0c8cba293631234f5ad940a14105172c795f2058027ab8450521f81f0301a01" :answer/id #uuid "938b8c44-0756-587a-98c2-8ca66c22427c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}12 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-81200/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "f3f8d76b-29d9-5db6-b00d-6b11a0911a16" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-81200/selection/c0c8cba293631234f5ad940a14105172c795f2058027ab8450521f81f0301a01" :answer-field/choices ["q-81200/selection/d75933ccdef909be74ce3d210a4b508b4ae0f3c90e8b68aa102024366905c0a6" "q-81200/selection/1fbf95c252312fea464880d0146235c2d254085faaec63a5ef8fe17552495710" "q-81200/selection/a3f9576cd5e49b32680167e2d19cb3084db80cef51740e2c74eee8b8d9070598" "q-81200/selection/b94ad2ce8b17f182e799d872f345298a72a9b827c3051416e0b84910de3366fc" "q-81200/selection/c0c8cba293631234f5ad940a14105172c795f2058027ab8450521f81f0301a01"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-81200" :question/id #uuid "8bc5c35e-337a-5a6f-8888-1b0686935cc0" :question/math-academy-id "q-81200" :question/problem "Given the vector $x$ and the system of linear equations below, find the projection of $x$ onto the solution space of the system.\n\n$$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}12 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-3{x}_{2}=0 \\\\ 3{x}_{1}-5{x}_{2}-8{x}_{3}=0\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to find a basis of the solution space of the system. \n\nConsider the augmented matrix $M$ of the system, which we reduce to row echelon form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 3 & -5 & -8 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4 & -8 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn the reduced matrix above, there are $2$ pivot columns ($1$st and $2$nd). Thus, ${x}_{3}$ is a free variable. Now, from the second equation, we get ${x}_{2}=2{x}_{3}.$ Substituting this into the first equation, we obtain \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}-3\\cdot (2{x}_{3})=0\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=6{x}_{3}.\n$$\n\nSo, the general solution is\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}6{x}_{3} \\\\ 2{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]={x}_{3}[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{3}\\in R.\n$$\n\nConsequently, $B={[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]}$ is a basis of the solution space of the system.\n\nFinally, we find the projection of $x$ onto the solution space of the system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{b}\\,x & =\\frac{x\\cdot b}{b\\cdot b}b \\\\  & =\\frac{12\\cdot 6+5\\cdot 2+0\\cdot 1}{{6}^{2}+{2}^{2}+{1}^{2}}b \\\\  & =\\frac{82}{41}b \\\\  & =2b \\\\  & =2[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}12 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-81200/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f8d8c7fb-e69a-5b52-9566-4d2e0c7e54fc"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-81200"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-40425"] :question/problem "Given the vector $x$ and the system of linear equations below, find the projection of $x$ onto the solution space of the system.\n\n$$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}11 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}],\\,{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=0 \\\\ 2{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}=0\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to find a basis of the solution space of the system. \n\nConsider the augmented matrix $M$ of the system, which we reduce to row echelon form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 2 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn the reduced matrix above, there is $1$ pivot column (the $1$st one). Thus, ${x}_{2}$ is a free variable. From the first equation, we get ${x}_{1}=-{x}_{2}.$ So, the general solution is\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-{x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]={x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{2}\\in R.\n$$\n\nConsequently, $B={[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]}$ is a basis of the solution space of the system.\n\nFinally, we find the projection of $x$ onto the solution space of the system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{b}\\,x & =\\frac{x\\cdot b}{b\\cdot b}b \\\\  & =\\frac{11\\cdot (-1)+3\\cdot 1}{{(-1)}^{2}+{1}^{2}}b \\\\  & =\\frac{-8}{2}b \\\\  & =-4b \\\\  & =-4[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-140119/selection/990e215d45312a763709abeb3c40d1b6f27667464c53da1245d32b1f77120b3d" :answer/id #uuid "bb060b3c-ce48-5925-9266-531aef721cdb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -6 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-140119/selection/9066abdb38501ddc17bb6ded91a6e00010c2ec816d6c3b81bc578b23eb459fce" :answer/id #uuid "8d944ace-c8c5-52d7-b560-796af07c4d3d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -6 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-140119/selection/166877bd2b5a5fc4f9a18a1b8dd48bc83cf34ab1c01727c9a38a1d43361ce79a" :answer/id #uuid "8e77f955-361d-5749-89d2-fa7e25e42e6c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-140119/selection/ff9d6c6d0d89ad9ca8de355ae092c794d7ec79dfc44e7972105de4e42d0d7133" :answer/id #uuid "e011a09b-a740-54a1-ba76-6e7fa3a541f7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -6 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-140119/selection/2ac3c07f46ddae25b284d9881e9bd8b68a558040ab4d435e0646ad7c10766fc1" :answer/id #uuid "7f4841d6-de1d-5c16-a723-4c57b0beb550" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-140119/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "c719a775-1b0d-5fc7-9055-195354f657a8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-140119/selection/9066abdb38501ddc17bb6ded91a6e00010c2ec816d6c3b81bc578b23eb459fce" :answer-field/choices ["q-140119/selection/990e215d45312a763709abeb3c40d1b6f27667464c53da1245d32b1f77120b3d" "q-140119/selection/9066abdb38501ddc17bb6ded91a6e00010c2ec816d6c3b81bc578b23eb459fce" "q-140119/selection/166877bd2b5a5fc4f9a18a1b8dd48bc83cf34ab1c01727c9a38a1d43361ce79a" "q-140119/selection/ff9d6c6d0d89ad9ca8de355ae092c794d7ec79dfc44e7972105de4e42d0d7133" "q-140119/selection/2ac3c07f46ddae25b284d9881e9bd8b68a558040ab4d435e0646ad7c10766fc1"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-140119" :question/id #uuid "b76f14de-8a84-5055-bcfe-22640334e836" :question/math-academy-id "q-140119" :question/problem "Given the vector $x$ and the system of linear equations below, find the projection of $x$ onto the solution space of the system.\n\n$$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}],\\,{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-{x}_{3}=0 \\\\ 2{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}=0\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to find a basis for the solution space of the system. \n\nConsider the augmented matrix $M$ of the system, which we reduce to row echelon form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn the reduced matrix above, there are $2$ pivot columns ($1$st and $2$nd). Thus, ${x}_{3}$ is a free variable. Now, from the first equation, we get ${x}_{1}={x}_{3}$ and from the second equation ${x}_{2}=-3{x}_{3}.$  \n\nSo, the general solution is\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{3} \\\\ -3{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]={x}_{3}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{3}\\in R.\n$$\n\nConsequently, $B={[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]}$ is a basis of the solution space of the system.\n\nFinally, we find the projection of $x$ onto the solution space of the system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{b}\\,x & =\\frac{x\\cdot b}{b\\cdot b}b \\\\  & =\\frac{3\\cdot 1+(-5)\\cdot (-3)+4\\cdot 1}{{1}^{2}+(-3)^{2}+{1}^{2}}b \\\\  & =\\frac{22}{11}b \\\\  & =2b \\\\  & =2[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -6 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-140119/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f8d8c7fb-e69a-5b52-9566-4d2e0c7e54fc"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-140119"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-5570"] :question/problem "Let ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14066555/assets/8a460dfb89b0d2e9c1e197aa212f494971df1c36822117fb4b1271f5608d1d1a.png) and ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14066555/assets/a172f54b0dc879c2363cfd2818fc79614d68662def6dd56b0ac9aec8fdbca1a5.png) Find the orthogonal projection of $\\mathbf{a}$ onto $\\text{Span}\\{\\mathbf{b}\\}.$" :question/worked-solution "The orthogonal projection of $\\mathbf{a}$ onto $\\textrm{Span}\\{\\mathbf{b}\\}$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{b}\\,a & =\\frac{b\\cdot a}{b\\cdot b}b \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\cdot 2+1\\cdot 9+0\\cdot (-1)+1\\cdot (-1)}{{2}^{2}+{1}^{2}+{0}^{2}+{1}^{2}}b \\\\  & =\\frac{4+9+0-1}{4+1+0+1}b \\\\  & =\\frac{12}{6}b \\\\  & =2b \\\\  & =2[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-5571"] :question/problem "Let ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14066555/assets/fb060fbc7ac20ff3b739a7c8958b4977e72abd31679c098973395db99fb6f78e.png) and ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14066555/assets/7a20f39cb1c7c36a01e9d7d4dcd8cbe619c8cffacb57bc2bf42b8d46ce53bb5b.png) If $\\mathbf{x} = \\mathbf{y} + \\mathbf{z},$ where $\\mathbf{y} \\in \\text{Span}\\{\\mathbf{a}\\}$ and $\\mathbf{z} \\perp \\text{Span}\\{\\mathbf{a}\\},$ then find $\\mathbf{z}.$" :question/worked-solution "A diagram of the situation is provided below:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14066555/assets/d887852fe51f08cb7296437e69b6a9632721cfd155558e6abf9a99b4f59f7ad6.png)\n\nFirst, we find the orthogonal projection of $\\mathbf{x}$ onto $\\textrm{Span}\\{\\mathbf{a}\\}\\mathbin{:}$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{a}\\,x & =\\frac{a\\cdot x}{a\\cdot a}a \\\\  & =\\frac{1\\cdot 4+(-1)\\cdot (-4)+0\\cdot 2+(-1)\\cdot 2}{{1}^{2}+(-1)^{2}+{0}^{2}+(-1)^{2}}a \\\\  & =\\frac{4+4+0-2}{1+1+0+1}a \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{3}a \\\\  & =2a \\\\  & =2[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, we get the following:  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & ={\\text{proj}}_{a}\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\ z & =x-{\\text{proj}}_{a}\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that $\\mathbf{y} \\in \\text{Span}\\{\\mathbf{a}\\}$ and $\\mathbf{z} \\perp \\text{Span}\\{\\mathbf{a}\\},$ as shown in the picture above." :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-5572"] :question/problem "Given the vector $\\mathbf{x}$ and the system of linear equations below, find the projection of $\\mathbf{x}$ onto the solution space of the system.\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14066555/assets/37beee87c5b5bd6350bd2c0f6353b61b1cfd321449a96b8b66aac99584d459bb.png)" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to find the basis of the solution space of the system. \n\nConsider the augmented matrix $M$ of the system, which we reduce to row echelon form, as follows:    \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -4 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn the reduced matrix above, there are $2$ pivot columns ($1$st and $2$nd). Thus, $x_3$ is a free variable. Now, from the second equation, we get $x_2=4x_3.$ \nSubstituting this into the first equation, we obtain  \n\n$$\nx_1+4x_3+4x_3= 0\n\\qquad\\Longrightarrow\\qquad\nx_1=-8x_3.\n$$\n\nSo, the general solution is\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14066555/assets/4995b9959cbb8a412fe0ed6198bfa9a82bcda40cd388c4759589e060ec16de1e.png)\nConsequently, ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14066555/assets/232c58060c7ba67f66564e8f8667fe67a84f6ef886a1c56e2d042224ace9b4db.png) is a basis of the solution space of the system.\n\nFinally, we find the projection of $\\mathbf{x}$ onto the solution space of the system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{b}\\,x & =\\frac{x\\cdot b}{b\\cdot b}b \\\\  & =\\frac{(-10)\\cdot (-8)+20\\cdot 4+2\\cdot 1}{{(-8)}^{2}+{4}^{2}+{1}^{2}}b \\\\  & =\\frac{80+80+2}{64+16+1}b \\\\  & =\\frac{162}{81}b \\\\  & =2b \\\\  & =2[\\begin{aligned}-8 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-16 \\\\ 8 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]}]
